-- title:
--   The index of nΛ in a rational quaternion order is n⁴
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b$ be rational numbers and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of the project's predicate `IsOrder`: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication of its elements, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and it is finitely generated as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module. Let $n$ be a natural number with $n>0$. Consider the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule generated by the image of $\Lambda$ under multiplication by $n$, that is the $\mathbb{Z}$-span of $\{\,n\cdot y : y\in\Lambda\,\}$, which is the submodule $n\Lambda$. The assertion is that the relative index of the underlying additive subgroup of this span inside the underlying additive subgroup of $\Lambda$ — the index of $n\Lambda$ in $\Lambda \cap n\Lambda$'s ambient group relative to $\Lambda$, i.e. the cardinality of $\Lambda/n\Lambda$ in the `AddSubgroup.relIndex` formulation — equals $n^4$.
--
--   This is the standard computation that an order in a quaternion algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$ is a free $\mathbb{Z}$-module of rank $4$, so that $\Lambda/n\Lambda$ has order $n^4$. It is used, in the relative-index bookkeeping shared with the statements about left ideals of maximal orders, in the level-structure and moduli lemmas for fake elliptic curves, where it yields the count $n^4$ for the $n$-torsion of an abelian surface with quaternionic multiplication.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_relIndex_span_smul_eq_pow_four.lean

